abla Cj(xi) is the gradient of the j-th constraint with respect to particle positions at xi. b. Compute Position Update (\Delta x): Update the primal variable (positions) based on the multiplier update. \Delta x \leftarrow M^{-1} 
abla C(xi)^	op \Delta \lambda This sums the contributions of all constraints to each particle's position. c. Update State: Update the multipliers and positions for the next iteration step. \lambda{i+1} \leftarrow \lambdai + \Delta \lambda x{i+1} \leftarrow xi + \Delta x 4. Finalize Step: Update the system state for the next time step. x{n+1} \leftarrow x{	ext{solverIterations}} v{n+1} \leftarrow  rac{x{n+1} - xn}{\Delta t} Formulas System Potential Energy: U =  rac{1}{2} C(x)^	op \alpha^{-1} C(x) where C(x) is the constraint vector and \alpha is the compliance matrix. Constraint Force Multiplier Update (General Form): \left[  rac{2}{\Delta t^2} 
