u}k, apply the 4D scale-adaptive filter. If the primitive is invisible at time t, dilation is avoided. The filter adjusts the dilation coefficient based on the ratio of Gaussian scales before and after temporal changes \Delta s(t) to preserve dimensional proportions and reduce anisotropy impact when st = s + \Delta s(t) approaches \hat{
u}k. 3. Incorporate 2D Mip Filter: Integrate the 2D Mip filter to address Gaussian scale mismatch in 4DGS, providing a general anti-aliasing solution. 4. Apply Scale Loss: Constrain the Gaussian's own scale to reduce filtering errors when the Gaussian scale is smaller than the filter scale. The regularization term is Gk(x){reg} =  rac{e^{- rac{1}{2}(x-pk)^T (\Sigmak + \sigmas^2 \cdot I)^{-1} (x-pk)}}{\sigmas \sqrt{|\Sigmak + \hat{
